 $4$ grams of garlic powder, among other ingredients, so she needs $\\boxed{}$ grams of ginger powder for each gram of garlic." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the number of grams of ginger powder to the number of grams of garlic powder is  $3:4.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\frac{3}{4}$ grams of ginger powder for each gram of garlic powder."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7435b531-e922-5db5-8140-463b7e66dd64" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Statement by Interpreting a Fraction as a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42896cb7-0d0b-54cc-969c-bb0fda2c6508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517618} {:answer/id #uuid "6cced7a0-4aa3-52bc-9f11-947258d1a3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$13$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517693} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac161ed-1d7c-54b3-a3a8-e7718d81f9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $13$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517722} {:answer/id #uuid "80b5563d-a832-5f85-beb1-f5023beb53ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517732} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6e0e18-3319-51dc-bd29-cc144c970a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80b5563d-a832-5f85-beb1-f5023beb53ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517732} :answer-field/id #uuid "adf5e13e-d3c5-59f6-8423-d12c85673faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fed5c231-48f8-530b-a66d-407d2c45633b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60250" :question/problem "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nA student makes a mixture having $\\frac{4}{9}$ grams of ginger for each gram of glucose to make his own energy drink. Therefore, the energy drink has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ grams of ginger to $\\boxed{}$ grams of glucose." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{4}{9}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n4:9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the energy drink has a ratio of $4$ grams of ginger to $9$ grams of glucose."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6a21dbe-0674-5fa2-b3ee-e4069115c6be" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4e2340-8ee0-5351-9fb5-c525dfce930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517520} {:answer/id #uuid "36eea84d-8adf-5277-ab85-88e996c1fbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517596} {:answer/id #uuid "3ccb5484-6c71-5479-8103-efc8575ddd3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517609} {:answer/id #uuid "c434fe79-4413-5270-a27f-9ddb3e2c1623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517863} {:answer/id #uuid "f9df7a6a-2bf6-55ee-9e50-cffb838757e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c434fe79-4413-5270-a27f-9ddb3e2c1623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517863} :answer-field/id #uuid "260e99a3-e5e1-53cf-915e-ef78d3294c9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517988}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c4f25cf-0173-54ec-98c6-ab10b632fa9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-60256" :question/problem "![](images/06/06931fae92045635d523614dce24063856209b1f04987471b9de183a3ccce4a2.png)\n\nIf the ratio of rhombuses to total shapes is $\\frac{3}{\\boxed{}}$ then what is the missing number?" :question/worked-solution "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $3$ rhombuses.\n\n We count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $7$ shapes.\n\nHence, the ratio of circles to triangles is$\\frac{3}{7}$\n\nSo the missing number is $7.$"}]}
